      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Recto",
          "value": "<ol>\n<li>In the name of God, the merciful and compassionate.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li>What do our lords, the jurisconsults, the im\u0101ms, im\u0101ms of the religion and model&nbsp;</li>\n<li>of the Muslims, may God grant them success for their obedience and assist them to gain his satisfaction, say concerning the following.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li>A group of Jews whose word is authoritative, namely&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li>the head of the Jews and those of their sages who are his followers, have established the practice of genuflection and prostration&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li>in their worship. They have stated that this was an ancient practice and that they have revived&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li>an aspect of worship that had fallen into disuse. They established and practiced it&nbsp; over a long period,&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li>amounting to approximately twenty years. When their head died,&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li>a man who was not a sage took office. He spoke against the earlier (opinion) of&nbsp;</li>\n<li>their sages and disapproved of genuflexion and prostration. What action should be&nbsp; taken with regard to him&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li>on account of his opposition, if he opposes (the practice). Grant us your opinion,&nbsp; may God have mercy upon you.&nbsp;</li>\n</ol>",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
        "sc:supplementing",
        "translating"
      ],
      "schema:position": 1
    },
